{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A planar embedding of a graph: a rotation system, the clockwise order of the edges around each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, over every edge position. Its faces satisfy Euler’s formula, n − m + f = 2, in every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected component with an edge.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding.swift#L66","fileName":"PlanarEmbedding.swift"},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}],"externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"PlanarEmbedding","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Faces.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before e in the clockwise order at w, so a face lies to the right of each of its half-edges."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated vertex has none: two disjoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triangles have four faces."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"]]},"topi